  "summary_en": "China's State Council Decree No. 831 promulgates the Water Supply Regulations, effective 1 June 2026, replacing the Urban Water Supply Regulations. It covers water sources, infrastructure construction, utility operations and service, facility protection, emergency management and penalties. It is unrelated to AI or robotics.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Effective 1 June 2026; replaces the Urban Water Supply Regulations.",
   "Water suppliers must be registered, meet capability conditions and test water quality regularly.",
   "Local governments bear primary responsibility for water supply security and emergency plans.",
   "Water supply facility information systems must follow cybersecurity rules and may be designated critical information infrastructure.",
   "Fines of up to RMB 500,000 for violations."
